  ($q$ei-471$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 2, $q$Early telescopes could resolve only the brightest stars. ______ modern instruments detect objects billions of light-years away.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Likewise,","Therefore,","Specifically,","However,"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The second sentence expresses contrast relative to the first sentence, so "However" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-472$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
