  ($q$ei-507$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$The company introduced a four-day workweek in 2022. ______ employee turnover fell by a third.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Nevertheless,","Similarly,","In addition,","Therefore,"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The second sentence expresses a cause-and-effect result relative to the first sentence, so "Therefore" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-508$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$Residents of the northern district largely supported the transit plan. ______ those in the southern district opposed it.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["However,","In the same way,","Subsequently,","Therefore,"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence expresses contrast relative to the first sentence, so "However" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-509$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$The volcano released ash across the region for several days. ______ airlines canceled hundreds of flights.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["For instance,","In the same way,","Thus,","Later,"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The second sentence expresses a cause-and-effect result relative to the first sentence, so "Thus" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-510$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 1, $q$Oak trees provide food for dozens of animal species. ______ their roots help prevent soil erosion.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["For example,","Furthermore,","Nevertheless,","Thus,"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The second sentence expresses an additional, supporting point relative to the first sentence, so "Furthermore" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-511$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• Bamboo is a type of grass.
