  ($q$ei-512$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
• The Library of Alexandria was founded in the third century BCE.
• It aimed to collect every book in the known world.
• Historians still debate exactly how and when it declined.$q$, $q$The student wants to describe when the library was founded and what it aimed to do. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$, $q$["Although the Library of Alexandria aimed to collect every book in the known world, historians still debate how and when it declined.","Founded in the third century BCE, the Library of Alexandria declined in ways that historians still debate.","Founded in the third century BCE, the Library of Alexandria aimed to collect every book in the known world.","Historians still debate exactly how and when the Library of Alexandria declined."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The goal calls for two specific pieces of information from the notes. This choice is the only one that includes both of them; each of the other choices omits one of them or relies on a note that is not relevant to the goal.$q$),
  ($q$ei-513$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 2, $q$Many scientists expected the reef to bleach completely after the heat wave. ______ large sections of the reef recovered within a year.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["However,","Specifically,","Similarly,","Afterward,"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence expresses contrast relative to the first sentence, so "However" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-514$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 2, $q$Kyoto limits the number of tourists allowed in its historic district. ______ Venice has introduced a fee for day visitors.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Specifically,","In the same way,","Consequently,","Subsequently,"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The second sentence expresses a similarity relative to the first sentence, so "In the same way" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-515$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
