  ($q$ei-519$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 2, $q$The team first collected soil samples from the riverbank. ______ they analyzed the samples in a laboratory in the city.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Later,","Thus,","Likewise,","In contrast,"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The second sentence expresses a sequence of events relative to the first sentence, so "Later" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-520$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Transitions$q$, 2, $q$The recycling program reduced landfill waste by nearly 20 percent. ______ it saved the city more than a million dollars in disposal fees.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$, $q$["Therefore,","Additionally,","Subsequently,","Nevertheless,"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The second sentence expresses an additional, supporting point relative to the first sentence, so "Additionally" is the logical transition. The other choices signal relationships the sentences do not have.$q$),
  ($q$ei-521$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Expression of Ideas$q$, $q$Rhetorical Synthesis$q$, 2, $q$A student has gathered the following notes:
